WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
The program behind the classroom. Inventory and selected-period activity answer different questions.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Nine lenses. Different questions. No-show. Completion. Timing. Retry patterns. Each has a calculation.

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Open the reasoning. The native explanation connects the measure, formula and variables.

4
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Make the number traceable. 1 qualifying empty run out of 25 valid runs. The interface shows 4%.

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Models need context. VRI includes a fixed 0.8 assumption. These are modeled indices, not causal proof.

6
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Know when comparison stops. Seven-day slice. No eligible peers. The gate is explicit.

7
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.500
Keep the absolute values. Activity remains visible. The app does not invent a fair peer comparison.

8
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:35.000
Give review work its context. Queue age. Grade distribution. Class and lesson detail.

9
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.500
Inspect the pattern. A class-by-lesson view keeps the individual values within reach.

10
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:42.500
Follow the learning sequence. Started. Submitted. Reviewed. Three states with different meanings.

11
00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:45.500
Return to the wider picture. A view across weeks. A path back to the work. Original app. Fictional data.
